%N A398287 Number of satisfiable 3-SAT formulas with 4 variables and n clauses in the multiset clause model.
%C A398287 Clauses are multisets of 3 literals chosen from {x_1, x_2, x_3, x_4, not x_1, ..., not x_4}; repeated literals inside a clause are allowed. A formula is a multiset of n such clauses, so repeated clauses are also allowed.
%D A398287 Stephen A. Cook, The complexity of theorem-proving procedures, Proceedings of the Third Annual ACM Symposium on Theory of Computing, 1971, 151-158.
%H A398287 <a href="/index/Rec#order_100">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, order 100.
%F A398287 a(n) = binomial(n+119,n) - A396351(4,n).
%F A398287 a(n) = 16*binomial(n+99,n) - 32*binomial(n+89,n) - 48*binomial(n+83,n) - 32*binomial(n+80,n) + 88*binomial(n+79,n) - 24*binomial(n+75,n) + 192*binomial(n+73,n) + 128*binomial(n+70,n) - 256*binomial(n+69,n) + 48*binomial(n+67,n) - 240*binomial(n+66,n) + 288*binomial(n+65,n) - 384*binomial(n+63,n) + 192*binomial(n+62,n) - 208*binomial(n+61,n) - 208*binomial(n+60,n) + 544*binomial(n+59,n) - 512*binomial(n+58,n) - 32*binomial(n+57,n) + 952*binomial(n+56,n) - 492*binomial(n+55,n) + 576*binomial(n+54,n) + 512*binomial(n+53,n) - 1376*binomial(n+52,n) + 840*binomial(n+51,n) - 320*binomial(n+50,n) - 1360*binomial(n+49,n) + 1696*binomial(n+48,n) - 1168*binomial(n+47,n) - 192*binomial(n+46,n) + 1536*binomial(n+45,n) - 1344*binomial(n+44,n) + 564*binomial(n+43,n) + 1824*binomial(n+42,n) - 2640*binomial(n+41,n) + 576*binomial(n+40,n) + 1120*binomial(n+39,n) - 1504*binomial(n+38,n) + 216*binomial(n+37,n) + 1216*binomial(n+36,n) - 1000*binomial(n+35,n) + 288*binomial(n+34,n) - 64*binomial(n+33,n) + 32*binomial(n+32,n) - 7*binomial(n+31,n).
